FIGURE's patch 2 of 5 to ImPlot3D (commit c54525f8d46cece384cc2618761a2c55016b06db, the submodule of cimplot3d v0.5).

ImDrawList3D kept its indices in Dear ImGui's ImDrawIdx (16-bit), so RenderPrimitivesEx drew, of a plot, only the
primitives that 65535 vertices hold: a 256 x 256 surface (4 vertices per cell) showed 16383 of its 65025 cells, the
rest silently dropped (#15, finding U1). The 3-D list's indices are now 32-bit (IdxBuffer, _IdxWritePtr: unsigned int;
the items' 30 index writes cast to unsigned int, not ImDrawIdx), its room MaxVtx() = 2^29 - 1 vertices (three indices
per vertex at most stay within ImVector's int). SortedMoveToImGuiDrawList keeps its path for a list of at most 65535
vertices; a larger one is moved as runs of sorted triangles, each triangle's three vertices written in the sorted
order (no index remap past 16 bits), a run one texture and at most MaxIdx() / 3 triangles, each run one PrimReserve,
which starts a draw command at a new VtxOffset when the window's list would pass 65535 vertices (Dear ImGui's
ImDrawFlags_UseVtxOffset, set by every renderer FIGURE has: OpenGL 3, the headless CPU one, the remote page); without
that flag the runs that fit are drawn. The depth order and the pixels of a list that fitted before are unchanged.
Applied to third_party/implot3d/implot3d_internal.h, implot3d.cpp, implot3d_items.cpp; without it
src/tests/fortran/figure_test_plot_frame_3d_big.F90 draws a quarter of its surface on the current path. To offer
upstream.

